# Backend production core

Source of truth: `Rules/NODEJS_POSTGRESQL_BACKEND_PRODUCTION_RULES.md`.

- Strict TypeScript; max 300 lines per maintained file; parameterized SQL only.
- No demos, fake WHMCS success, mock repositories in production paths, or TODO behavior.
- WHMCS owns customers, access, pricing, orders, billing — Postgres caches and local content only.
- Idempotency + tenant scope (`whmcs_client_id`) on every customer mutation/read of private data.
- Secrets server-only; never log API secrets, passwords, or raw payment payloads.
